{"author_date": "2026-07-09T17:20:01Z", "author_login": "haakon-e", "commit_date": "2026-07-09T17:20:01Z", "committer_login": "haakon-e", "message": "feat: make data-backed profiles isbits for device broadcast\n\nReplace the shared linear_interp helper's Interpolations.jl backing\n(Gridded(Linear)/Flat over host Vectors, non-isbits) with\nClimaInterpolations.Interpolation1D.Interpolate1D (Linear/Flat) over\nStaticArrays SVector knot and value storage. All 32 data-backed profile\nconstructors route through this helper, so the conversion is uniform;\nsignatures, knots, linear interpolation and flat extrapolation are\nunchanged. ClimaAtmos captures these profile callables in structs that\nare broadcast to the device, which requires the callables to be isbits.\n\nValues match the previous implementation to machine epsilon rather than\nbitwise, due to the barycentric arithmetic ordering in Interpolate1D.\n\nValidation: the full test suite passes; isbits holds for every profile\ncallable except the out-of-scope two-dimensional TRMM_LBA_radiation,\nwhich retains its Interpolations.jl backing; a dense sweep over a\nrepresentative sample (Bomex_tke_prescribed, GATE_III T/q_tot/u/dTdt,\nTRMM_LBA T/u/v/RH, Larcform1_RH, ARM_SGP) agrees with the previous\nimplementation to machine epsilon.", "sha": "3c6f2818316795f4bd03f70aea72bc3f91c74ace"}
